1
00:00:03,082 --> 00:00:04,862
In the pot, it goes pop, pop!

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:08,018
The small hard kernels turn into big white clouds…

3
00:00:08,068 --> 00:00:09,962
but what is going on in there?

4
00:00:10,782 --> 00:00:13,346
Mila looks at a kernel with a magnifying glass:

5
00:00:13,396 --> 00:00:15,626
a hard shell, all smooth, tightly closed.

6
00:00:15,676 --> 00:00:17,684
And inside, a little water is hiding…

7
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:18,568
that's the key!

8
00:00:19,342 --> 00:00:20,856
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,372 --> 00:00:23,968
Mini mode!

10
00:00:24,018 --> 00:00:27,263
Inside the kernel, there is starch, a little water,

11
00:00:27,313 --> 00:00:29,202
and all around, a solid shell.

12
00:00:29,252 --> 00:00:32,095
When we heat it, the water turns into steam.

13
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:35,682
This steam wants to get out, but the shell is closed,

14
00:00:35,732 --> 00:00:37,398
so the pressure rises and rises…

15
00:00:37,448 --> 00:00:39,597
and at around one hundred eighty degrees,

16
00:00:39,647 --> 00:00:40,558
the shell cracks!

17
00:00:41,892 --> 00:00:43,785
All at once, the pressure drops,

18
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:47,731
and the soft starch puffs up like foam, then hardens as it cools…

19
00:00:47,781 --> 00:00:49,724
it's a white flake, much bigger!

20
00:00:50,514 --> 00:00:52,317
And the kernels that don't pop?

21
00:00:52,367 --> 00:00:54,946
Their shell is cracked, or they are too dry,

22
00:00:54,996 --> 00:00:56,679
so the pressure doesn't rise…

23
00:00:56,729 --> 00:00:57,147
no pop!

24
00:00:57,930 --> 00:01:00,191
And that's why popcorn pops.

25
00:01:01,448 --> 00:01:04,794
The water in the kernel turns to steam, the pressure cracks the shell,

26
00:01:04,844 --> 00:01:06,494
and the starch puffs up into foam.

27
00:01:07,430 --> 00:01:08,303
With an adult:

28
00:01:08,353 --> 00:01:10,807
watch the kernels through a glass lid.

29
00:01:10,857 --> 00:01:11,796
Count the pops…

30
00:01:11,846 --> 00:01:14,614
and look for the hard shell on each flake!

31
00:01:15,401 --> 00:01:16,901
And what do we breathe?

32
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,299
The answer tomorrow.
